From 992c274696d308a9a0d8aa4e1e761982ad9926e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adpena <adpena@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:36:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Reject unregistered operations through generated frontend and
 SimpleIR admission

The CONST_MISSING regression in fd670c00a exposed a preexisting admission
defect: frontend serialization ignored its final dispatch result, SimpleIR
accepted arbitrary kind strings, and SSA preserved unmapped kinds as Copy.
A resultless unknown operation could then compile natively without emission.
The instance was repaired in 9a5babb29; this change closes the class.

Derive wire and frontend membership from op_kinds.toml's existing mapper,
control, classifier, field-role and semantic registrations. Explicitly
register existing cast/widen/unreachable carriers and frontend serializer
spellings without changing their effect or target-support contracts.
Regenerate Rust/Python projections and proof-plan authority freshness.

Validate frontend kinds before and after optimization, require successful
serializer dispatch, and validate emitted wire kinds. Share one function-aware
Rust admission validator across all SimpleIR transports and direct SSA entry.
Retain precise retired-kind diagnostics and existing preserved-op semantics.

Add transport/programmatic Rust rejection tests and an AST frontend literal
scan, including serializer and optimizer regressions. Migrate fictitious
roundtrip operations to registered preserved carriers without removing their
metadata/SSA assertions. Replace unsupported is_truthy's negative bool fixture
with a registered opaque-result operation, retaining the independent oracle.

Also: encode guarded child stdin with the declared codec, not the locale.
memory_guard.run_guarded opened its stdin pipe with Popen(text=True) and no
encoding, so on Windows every guarded child received text input in the
locale code page (cp1252) while its captured stdout/stderr used UTF-8.
Non-ASCII input was corrupted: tools/gen_op_kinds.py --check piped its
generated Rust (with em dashes in doc comments) into rustfmt, which failed
with "stream did not contain valid UTF-8", so the op-kind generator and its
64 dependent tests could not run on Windows at all.

Pass the guard's encoding/errors to Popen whenever text mode is on, and let
ProcessSpawnKwargs carry them. Verified on Windows x86_64:

Verification (Windows x86_64, independently re-run): gen_op_kinds.py --check
in sync; frontend op-kind registry, op-kind generator, context-unwind and
memory-guard tool modules 629 passed, 23 skipped. Worker-reported: molt-ir
386 passed, molt-passes 949 passed. Two molt-tir failures
(generic_const_non_integer_payload_stays_outside_integer_admission,
loop_body_ops_survive_optimization) reproduce without this change and are
fixed separately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
